{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01257",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.14,
      "end_seconds": 7.31,
      "duration_seconds": 6.17,
      "text": "Erm, you know, morning, doctor. Is this the right room?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.4,
      "end_seconds": 12.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "Yes, have a seat. Tell me what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.19,
      "end_seconds": 21.43,
      "duration_seconds": 7.24,
      "text": "oh, so the thing is, I've got a high fever with shaking chills"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.73,
      "end_seconds": 31.07,
      "duration_seconds": 9.34,
      "text": "I follow. Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.83,
      "end_seconds": 44.8,
      "duration_seconds": 11.97,
      "text": "I get some relief from paracetamol it's worse with evenings i've been putting this off for weeks i've also been sweating a lot"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.42,
      "end_seconds": 48.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "What about muscle aches, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.01,
      "end_seconds": 60.33,
      "duration_seconds": 7.32,
      "text": "Yes, actually. As for muscle aches, pretty mild, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.51,
      "end_seconds": 68.13,
      "duration_seconds": 6.62,
      "text": "have you had a high fever with shaking chills before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 69.16,
      "end_seconds": 76.86,
      "duration_seconds": 7.7,
      "text": "yes, something like this happened last winter, and it it went away on its own"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 78.16,
      "end_seconds": 86.18,
      "duration_seconds": 8.02,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Oxygen saturation is 95 percent, pulse 94, BP is 115 over 76."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.12,
      "end_seconds": 88.82,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.02,
      "end_seconds": 95.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.8,
      "text": "I'd like to check you over now, if that's alright"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.32,
      "end_seconds": 100.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "Yeah, um, no problem."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.38,
      "end_seconds": 102.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.23,
      "text": "breathe out slowly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.83,
      "end_seconds": 120.22,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "The spleen tip is just palpable and the chest is clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.94,
      "end_seconds": 130.74,
      "duration_seconds": 4.8,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me. Have you had any rash or cough?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.08,
      "end_seconds": 135.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "No, um, no rash or cough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.53,
      "end_seconds": 141.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "did you get yellow eyes, neck stiffness or diarrhoea?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.92,
      "end_seconds": 147.63,
      "duration_seconds": 5.71,
      "text": "Oh, no, no yellow eyes, neck stiffness or diarrhoea."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.47,
      "end_seconds": 153.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "any change in your bowel habit or your stomach generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.06,
      "end_seconds": 157.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Ah, no, that side's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.0,
      "end_seconds": 161.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Any breathing difficulties apart from this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.43,
      "end_seconds": 166.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "No, my breathing's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.32,
      "end_seconds": 171.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.17,
      "end_seconds": 176.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "No, I've always been fairly healthy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.76,
      "end_seconds": 182.17,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "let's talk a little about your daily life and habits"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.28,
      "end_seconds": 195.06,
      "duration_seconds": 11.78,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days. I work in accounts at a hospital. I'm vegetarian and have been for years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.65,
      "end_seconds": 205.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.36,
      "end_seconds": 209.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "No, I've never been operated on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.5,
      "end_seconds": 212.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "let's run through your medicines"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.63,
      "end_seconds": 220.07,
      "duration_seconds": 5.44,
      "text": "It's Dolo, 650 milligrams, when I get the fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.69,
      "end_seconds": 248.37,
      "duration_seconds": 13.68,
      "text": "So where does that leave us? This is probably a fever after travel that must be treated as possible malaria. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 249.46,
      "end_seconds": 253.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "So, I'm scared it's something bad. Is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.88,
      "end_seconds": 271.63,
      "duration_seconds": 12.75,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's a fever after travel that must be treated as possible malaria, and we'll know more once the blood cultures is back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.83,
      "end_seconds": 304.01,
      "duration_seconds": 20.18,
      "text": "I want blood cultures done, that's for fever. Avoid anti-inflammatory painkillers and keep drinking. Cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle. I think the tropical diseases unit should see you too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 304.6,
      "end_seconds": 307.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "Sure, where do I go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.46,
      "end_seconds": 311.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "I'd like you back in two days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 315.49,
      "end_seconds": 319.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "I'll note it in my calendar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.96,
      "end_seconds": 324.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 326.11,
      "end_seconds": 330.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.68,
      "text": "hmm, I think I understand everything. Thanks"
    }
  ]
}